{#
  The other two games, as rows at the foot of a game page. Rows rather than
  the hub's big cards because this sits under the FAQ.

  Icons are the lobby blink characters, loaded as <img> so each keeps its own
  animation and its own document, which is what stops the Figma ids inside
  them colliding with the page's inline hero.

  Which games appear is data and which of them EXIST is not: the build
  resolves this list per locale (`otherGames` in build.mjs), dropping any game
  with no page in this language and folding in its icon and its href. So the
  macro takes one already-correct list and renders it. It is deliberately not
  handed `site`: a template that can reach the raw href map is a template that
  can render an English path onto a Spanish page, which is #158.
#}
{% macro altGames(games) %}
<div class="alt-games">
{% for g in games %}
          <a class="alt-game {{ g.id }}" href="{{ g.href }}" aria-label="{{ g.aria | safe }}">
            <span class="alt-game-icon"><img src="{{ g.icon }}" alt="" width="{{ g.iconW }}" height="{{ g.iconH }}" loading="lazy" /></span>
            <span class="alt-game-name">{{ g.name | safe }}</span>
            <span class="alt-game-play">{{ g.play | safe }}</span>
          </a>
{% endfor %}
        </div>
{% endmacro %}
